{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xqr7qmBppiQtvRNtULJJTC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Queensland Electric Super Highway Yurika chargers app pay how to charge\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Welcome to the Queensland Electric Super Highway\",\"url\":\"https://www.yurika.com.au/capability/qld-electric-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"Yurika EV Charging Network\",\"url\":\"https://evlog.net.au/yurika-ev-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH) - Yurika\",\"url\":\"https://www.yurika.com.au/case-study/queensland-electric-super-highway-qesh/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging & Roadside Assistance in Brisbane\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/locations/brisbane/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric car drivers can now use Chargefox network from Adelaide to Cairns\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2019/07/02/electric-car-drivers-can-now-use-chargefox-network-from-adelaide-to-cairns/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/\"},{\"title\":\"Third phase of EV Super Highway to add 23 new charging stations\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2024/01/15/third-phase-of-ev-super-highway-to-add-23-new-charging-stations/\"},{\"title\":\"Chargefox extends EV network to the Queensland super highway\",\"url\":\"https://autotalk.com.au/industry-news/chargefox-extends-ev-network-queensland-super-highway\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland’s electric super highway to expand to over 30 electric car chargers\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2019/05/31/queensland-s-electric-super-highway-to-expand-to-over-50-electric-car-chargers/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric dreaming: Discover the 109 EV charging stations in Queensland - Flare\",\"url\":\"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/exploring-ev-charging-stations-in-queensland\"}]\n\nTo charge on the Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH), you use the Chargefox app. The network is run by Yurika, but Chargefox handles payment.\n\n**How to charge**\n- Yurika's official page says to get charging you'll need the Chargefox App, which you can download for iPhone or Android. You'll need to create an account before you plug in and start charging. The app shows how your charge is going in real time, so you don't need to keep checking back.\n- A Chargefox RFID card also works. An EV directory lists activation by the Chargefox app or RFID, with no Autocharge.\n- Connectors: DC charging uses CHAdeMO and CCS Combo Type 2 cables. AC charging uses a Type 2 Mennekes socket, and you bring your own cable. Each DC charger has a backup AC charger, which also needs your own Type 2 cable.\n- Help: visit www.chargefox.com or call 1300 518 038.\n\n**Cost**\n- Pricing varies by location. As a general guideline, slower chargers usually cost less and faster chargers usually cost more. Current prices and locations are in the Chargefox app. None of the results gave a current per-kWh rate. The last figure I found was from January 2020, when a 20c/kWh fee was introduced, so it's likely out of date.\n\n**Background and trip planning**\n- The QESH is a Queensland Government initiative, built and operated by Yurika and supported by RACQ. It has over 50 charging stations from Coolangatta to Port Douglas, extending into regional Queensland.\n- For route planning, Yurika recommends the PlugShare Trip Planner, which also shows whether stations are currently working.\n\nSources: yurika.com.au/capability/qld-electric-super-highway/ (updated about a month ago) and evlog.net.au.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"2c093264-6c83-40bf-9880-6c284d8adfb8","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:45:07.959Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Queensland Electric Super Highway Yurika chargers app pay how to charge","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01W2SLFRVog8dpfybSY9TR76","content":[{"title":"Welcome to the Queensland Electric Super Highway","url":"https://www.yurika.com.au/capability/qld-electric-super-highway/"},{"title":"Yurika EV Charging Network","url":"https://evlog.net.au/yurika-ev-charging-network/"},{"title":"Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH) - Yurika","url":"https://www.yurika.com.au/case-study/queensland-electric-super-highway-qesh/"},{"title":"EV Charging & Roadside Assistance in Brisbane","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/locations/brisbane/"},{"title":"Electric car drivers can now use Chargefox network from Adelaide to Cairns","url":"https://thedriven.io/2019/07/02/electric-car-drivers-can-now-use-chargefox-network-from-adelaide-to-cairns/"},{"title":"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout","url":"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/"},{"title":"Third phase of EV Super Highway to add 23 new charging stations","url":"https://thedriven.io/2024/01/15/third-phase-of-ev-super-highway-to-add-23-new-charging-stations/"},{"title":"Chargefox extends EV network to the Queensland super highway","url":"https://autotalk.com.au/industry-news/chargefox-extends-ev-network-queensland-super-highway"},{"title":"Queensland’s electric super highway to expand to over 30 electric car chargers","url":"https://thedriven.io/2019/05/31/queensland-s-electric-super-highway-to-expand-to-over-50-electric-car-chargers/"},{"title":"Electric dreaming: Discover the 109 EV charging stations in Queensland - Flare","url":"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/exploring-ev-charging-stations-in-queensland"}]},"To charge on the Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH), you use the Chargefox app. The network is run by Yurika, but Chargefox handles payment.\n\n**How to charge**\n- Yurika's official page says to get charging you'll need the Chargefox App, which you can download for iPhone or Android. You'll need to create an account before you plug in and start charging. The app shows how your charge is going in real time, so you don't need to keep checking back.\n- A Chargefox RFID card also works. An EV directory lists activation by the Chargefox app or RFID, with no Autocharge.\n- Connectors: DC charging uses CHAdeMO and CCS Combo Type 2 cables. AC charging uses a Type 2 Mennekes socket, and you bring your own cable. Each DC charger has a backup AC charger, which also needs your own Type 2 cable.\n- Help: visit www.chargefox.com or call 1300 518 038.\n\n**Cost**\n- Pricing varies by location. As a general guideline, slower chargers usually cost less and faster chargers usually cost more. Current prices and locations are in the Chargefox app. None of the results gave a current per-kWh rate. The last figure I found was from January 2020, when a 20c/kWh fee was introduced, so it's likely out of date.\n\n**Background and trip planning**\n- The QESH is a Queensland Government initiative, built and operated by Yurika and supported by RACQ. It has over 50 charging stations from Coolangatta to Port Douglas, extending into regional Queensland.\n- For route planning, Yurika recommends the PlugShare Trip Planner, which also shows whether stations are currently working.\n\nSources: yurika.com.au/capability/qld-electric-super-highway/ (updated about a month ago) and evlog.net.au."],"durationSeconds":9.437317186,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xqr7qmBppiQtvRNtULJJTC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PqoYtCc3sAFzS5fYA1Cwrx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Charging the Regions\" Victoria fast chargers app Evie\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Charging the Regions\",\"url\":\"https://www.cvga.org.au/charging-the-regions.html\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Vehicle Charging\",\"url\":\"https://www.wellington.vic.gov.au/environment/electric-vehicle-charging\"},{\"title\":\"Victoria Charging the Regions EV network\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/victoria-charging-the-regions-ev-network.203235/page-3\"},{\"title\":\"Charging the Regions 2\",\"url\":\"https://www.cvga.org.au/charging-the-regions-2.html\"},{\"title\":\"Evie steps up fast-charger network starting at Hungry Jacks - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2021/11/08/evie-steps-up-fast-charger-network-starting-at-hungry-jacks/\"},{\"title\":\"Victoria Charging the Regions EV network\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/victoria-charging-the-regions-ev-network.203235/page-8\"},{\"title\":\"Destination Charging Across Victoria Program\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/destination-charging-across-victoria-program.249073/\"},{\"title\":\"Victoria Charging the Regions EV network\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/victoria-charging-the-regions-ev-network.203235/page-4\"},{\"title\":\"High-tech rapid EV charger hits Central Victoria - Energy Magazine\",\"url\":\"https://www.energymagazine.com.au/high-tech-rapid-ev-charger-hits-central-victoria/\"},{\"title\":\"What if networks dropped kerbside charging access fees, and actually switched them on? - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2026/04/08/what-if-networks-dropped-kerbside-charging-access-fees-and-actually-switched-them-on/\"}]\n\nCharging the Regions (CTR) is a Victorian program for public EV fast charging, and Evie Networks runs and bills its chargers, so drivers use the Evie app.\n\n**The program**\n- CTR is a long-running effort to expand public EV charging across regional Victoria, led by the Central Victorian Greenhouse Alliance (CVGA) and local councils. The CVGA describes it as accelerating the rollout of public electric vehicle charging across regional Victoria.\n- In Stage 2b (2022–2024), it installed a dense network of 23 fast-charging stations from Whittlesea to Mildura. Evie Networks was contracted for operation and maintenance of the installed chargers.\n- Partner councils include Mildura, Swan Hill, Campaspe, Loddon, Central Goldfields, Gannawarra, Buloke, Macedon Ranges, Mount Alexander, Greater Bendigo, Greater Shepparton, Wellington and Whittlesea.\n\n**App and payment**\n- Forum users on Tesla Motors Club reported that all the CTR stations to date are on Evie's billing system, and that Evie provides billing for Charging the Regions (North-west Vic).\n- Wellington Shire Council says its chargers cost 40c/kWh, paid through either the Evie or Chargefox apps, depending on the location. That page is about four years old, so the price may have changed.\n- When the first sites opened, users said the sites are free at the moment according to the Evie app.\n\n**Charger speeds**\n- In 2021, The Driven reported that the CTR network Evie manages can charge at a rate of 31-45.6kW adding up to around 300-500km driving range an hour.\n- Some early sites were slower. For example, CTR Harcourt uses a 25kW Delta DC charger.\n- Maryborough got a Tritium RT-M unit. The Victorian Government invested $664,000 for these chargers.\n\nMost of these sources are from 2020–2022. The CVGA program pages are the most current, but they don't list current prices.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"50ce15f0-49c2-4c1c-967a-ef7906c55ea6","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:45:09.760Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"\"Charging the Regions\" Victoria fast chargers app Evie","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DUtiBnfRvvVU46Fxi8D9sY","content":[{"title":"Charging the Regions","url":"https://www.cvga.org.au/charging-the-regions.html"},{"title":"Electric Vehicle Charging","url":"https://www.wellington.vic.gov.au/environment/electric-vehicle-charging"},{"title":"Victoria Charging the Regions EV network","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/victoria-charging-the-regions-ev-network.203235/page-3"},{"title":"Charging the Regions 2","url":"https://www.cvga.org.au/charging-the-regions-2.html"},{"title":"Evie steps up fast-charger network starting at Hungry Jacks - The Driven","url":"https://thedriven.io/2021/11/08/evie-steps-up-fast-charger-network-starting-at-hungry-jacks/"},{"title":"Victoria Charging the Regions EV network","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/victoria-charging-the-regions-ev-network.203235/page-8"},{"title":"Destination Charging Across Victoria Program","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/destination-charging-across-victoria-program.249073/"},{"title":"Victoria Charging the Regions EV network","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/victoria-charging-the-regions-ev-network.203235/page-4"},{"title":"High-tech rapid EV charger hits Central Victoria - Energy Magazine","url":"https://www.energymagazine.com.au/high-tech-rapid-ev-charger-hits-central-victoria/"},{"title":"What if networks dropped kerbside charging access fees, and actually switched them on? - The Driven","url":"https://thedriven.io/2026/04/08/what-if-networks-dropped-kerbside-charging-access-fees-and-actually-switched-them-on/"}]},"Charging the Regions (CTR) is a Victorian program for public EV fast charging, and Evie Networks runs and bills its chargers, so drivers use the Evie app.\n\n**The program**\n- CTR is a long-running effort to expand public EV charging across regional Victoria, led by the Central Victorian Greenhouse Alliance (CVGA) and local councils. The CVGA describes it as accelerating the rollout of public electric vehicle charging across regional Victoria.\n- In Stage 2b (2022–2024), it installed a dense network of 23 fast-charging stations from Whittlesea to Mildura. Evie Networks was contracted for operation and maintenance of the installed chargers.\n- Partner councils include Mildura, Swan Hill, Campaspe, Loddon, Central Goldfields, Gannawarra, Buloke, Macedon Ranges, Mount Alexander, Greater Bendigo, Greater Shepparton, Wellington and Whittlesea.\n\n**App and payment**\n- Forum users on Tesla Motors Club reported that all the CTR stations to date are on Evie's billing system, and that Evie provides billing for Charging the Regions (North-west Vic).\n- Wellington Shire Council says its chargers cost 40c/kWh, paid through either the Evie or Chargefox apps, depending on the location. That page is about four years old, so the price may have changed.\n- When the first sites opened, users said the sites are free at the moment according to the Evie app.\n\n**Charger speeds**\n- In 2021, The Driven reported that the CTR network Evie manages can charge at a rate of 31-45.6kW adding up to around 300-500km driving range an hour.\n- Some early sites were slower. For example, CTR Harcourt uses a 25kW Delta DC charger.\n- Maryborough got a Tritium RT-M unit. The Victorian Government invested $664,000 for these chargers.\n\nMost of these sources are from 2020–2022. The CVGA program pages are the most current, but they don't list current prices."],"durationSeconds":10.390038004,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PqoYtCc3sAFzS5fYA1Cwrx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wodh8qEyQe48r9MQX716yq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"RAA electric vehicle charging network app Chargefox South Australia\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV charging stations\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicles\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/ev-hub\"},{\"title\":\"RAA completes South Australia’s first statewide EV charging network - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-completes-south-australias-first-statewide-ev-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"First \\\"border-to-border\\\" EV charging network for South Australia launches first 12 sites - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2023/03/02/first-border-to-border-ev-charging-network-for-south-australia-launches-first-12-sites/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA SA Charging Network\",\"url\":\"https://evlog.net.au/raa-sa-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"Chargefox builds rapid EV network for South Australians\",\"url\":\"https://www.evcandi.com/news/chargefox-builds-rapid-ev-network-south-australians\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Apps for EVs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/10/27/best-ev-charging-apps-for-evs-in-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"techAU interviews RAA: new South Australia EV charger network feat Kempower, Chargefox, JET Charge\",\"url\":\"https://techau.com.au/techau-interviews-raa-new-south-australia-electric-car-charger-network-feat-kempower-chargefox-jet-charge/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charge\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-12-electric-vehicle-charging-locations-switched-on-today-as-part-of-network-launch/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA expands EV charging network at four city UPark locations - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-expands-ev-charging-network-at-four-city-upark-locations/\"}]\n\nRAA's charging network in South Australia is called RAA Charge. It runs entirely on the Chargefox app, which you use to find a charger, start it and pay.\n\n**How the app fits in**\n- You find a site, charge and pay in the Chargefox app, or with an RFID card. Step 1: download Chargefox for iOS or Android. Step 2: find your nearest RAA Charge site in the app or on RAA's interactive map. Step 3: charge your EV and pay through the app or with your RFID card.\n- RAA's own member app shows charger locations, details and prices on a map, but you can't use it to start a charge. Any RFID card added to your Chargefox app will work.\n- Chargefox belongs to Australian Motoring Services (AMS) and provides the software, driver support and management services for the network.\n\n**Network size and history**\n- The first 12 sites opened in early 2023, built by Chargefox in partnership with the South Australian Government.\n- RAA says it has completed the network: more than 550 plugs at 144 charging sites, from Yalata to Mount Gambier. The State Government gave RAA a $12.35 million grant to build and run it.\n- RAA calls it SA's largest electric vehicle charging network. A third-party site counted 59 DC charging locations and 142 sites with AC charging (from RAA's charger locator, 1-8-2026).\n\n**Pricing and fees**\n- RAA members get 10% off, but only if a valid membership number is added to their Chargefox profile before the charging session starts.\n- Member prices are Metro AC 40c/kWh at peak (5pm–10pm) and 33c/kWh off-peak; Metro DC 75c/66c; Country AC 42c/35c; Country DC 76c/68c.\n- Idle fees apply at all DC rapid sites in SA. After a 10-minute grace period once charging finishes, it's $1 per minute if you stay plugged in.\n\n**Hardware**\n- AC sites (7kW–22kW) have Type 2 sockets, so you need your own cable. DC sites (60–200kW) have cables attached.\n- Rapid and ultra-rapid chargers use CCS 2 plugs, and some sites also have CHAdeMO.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"e484b31a-fcf9-4273-a998-9f3a67bae176","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:45:10.245Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"RAA electric vehicle charging network app Chargefox South Australia","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Ct4WQ25WDqJYAnuyXWTGsz","content":[{"title":"EV charging stations","url":"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations"},{"title":"Electric vehicles","url":"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/ev-hub"},{"title":"RAA completes South Australia’s first statewide EV charging network - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-completes-south-australias-first-statewide-ev-charging-network/"},{"title":"First \"border-to-border\" EV charging network for South Australia launches first 12 sites - The Driven","url":"https://thedriven.io/2023/03/02/first-border-to-border-ev-charging-network-for-south-australia-launches-first-12-sites/"},{"title":"RAA SA Charging Network","url":"https://evlog.net.au/raa-sa-charging-network/"},{"title":"Chargefox builds rapid EV network for South Australians","url":"https://www.evcandi.com/news/chargefox-builds-rapid-ev-network-south-australians"},{"title":"EV Charging Apps for EVs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/10/27/best-ev-charging-apps-for-evs-in-australia/"},{"title":"techAU interviews RAA: new South Australia EV charger network feat Kempower, Chargefox, JET Charge","url":"https://techau.com.au/techau-interviews-raa-new-south-australia-electric-car-charger-network-feat-kempower-chargefox-jet-charge/"},{"title":"RAA Charge","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-12-electric-vehicle-charging-locations-switched-on-today-as-part-of-network-launch/"},{"title":"RAA expands EV charging network at four city UPark locations - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-expands-ev-charging-network-at-four-city-upark-locations/"}]},"RAA's charging network in South Australia is called RAA Charge. It runs entirely on the Chargefox app, which you use to find a charger, start it and pay.\n\n**How the app fits in**\n- You find a site, charge and pay in the Chargefox app, or with an RFID card. Step 1: download Chargefox for iOS or Android. Step 2: find your nearest RAA Charge site in the app or on RAA's interactive map. Step 3: charge your EV and pay through the app or with your RFID card.\n- RAA's own member app shows charger locations, details and prices on a map, but you can't use it to start a charge. Any RFID card added to your Chargefox app will work.\n- Chargefox belongs to Australian Motoring Services (AMS) and provides the software, driver support and management services for the network.\n\n**Network size and history**\n- The first 12 sites opened in early 2023, built by Chargefox in partnership with the South Australian Government.\n- RAA says it has completed the network: more than 550 plugs at 144 charging sites, from Yalata to Mount Gambier. The State Government gave RAA a $12.35 million grant to build and run it.\n- RAA calls it SA's largest electric vehicle charging network. A third-party site counted 59 DC charging locations and 142 sites with AC charging (from RAA's charger locator, 1-8-2026).\n\n**Pricing and fees**\n- RAA members get 10% off, but only if a valid membership number is added to their Chargefox profile before the charging session starts.\n- Member prices are Metro AC 40c/kWh at peak (5pm–10pm) and 33c/kWh off-peak; Metro DC 75c/66c; Country AC 42c/35c; Country DC 76c/68c.\n- Idle fees apply at all DC rapid sites in SA. After a 10-minute grace period once charging finishes, it's $1 per minute if you stay plugged in.\n\n**Hardware**\n- AC sites (7kW–22kW) have Type 2 sockets, so you need your own cable. DC sites (60–200kW) have cables attached.\n- Rapid and ultra-rapid chargers use CCS 2 plugs, and some sites also have CHAdeMO."],"durationSeconds":11.275921874000002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wodh8qEyQe48r9MQX716yq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
