doesn't appear to impact their arrangement with Chargefox for activating/billing. Another snippet says NRMA owns all of the electric highway Tasmania's electric vehicle charging sites and suggests for real-time updates on individual chargers please check the Chargefox app. These two claims don't agree, so who owns the network now isn't clear.\n- **Hardware and pricing (from an early AEVA presentation, likely out of date):** Sites were planned with a 50 kW DC Tritium charger and a 22 kW AC charger. Pricing was 50 kW DC: 25 cents / minute + 25 cents / kWh.\n\nMost of these sources are old forum posts and user-edited PlugShare listings, so current payment options and prices should be checked in the Chargefox app."],"durationSeconds":9.792206686000005,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YYPyUkDsRd1Gnc93RKNPvX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013eJ2BUKhtgcy87h82VEgys","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WA EV Network Synergy Horizon Power chargers app Chargefox price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The cost to charge electric cars: Your local guide to EV charging costs in WA\",\"url\":\"https://www.synergy.net.au/Blog/2023/03/Cost-to-charge-EV-in-WA\"},{\"title\":\"State of Charge: The Complete Guide to Australia’s EV Charging Networks in 2026 - evee AU - Electric Car Rental\",\"url\":\"https://pages.evee.com.au/blog/state-of-charge-guide-australia-ev-charging-networks-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Electricity fees & charges - Horizon Power\",\"url\":\"https://www.horizonpower.com.au/utilities/pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"synergy.net.au CONSTRUCTION NOTICE LETTER\",\"url\":\"https://www.northam.wa.gov.au/Profiles/northam/Assets/ClientData/News/EV_NETWORK/Northam_-_WA_EV_Network_-_Letter_to_Residents_or_Business_Owners.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Horizon Power\",\"url\":\"https://www.horizonpower.com.au/about-us/news-announcements/fees-and-charges-2025/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Cost per kWh Australia 2026 — Home, Public & Solar Rates\",\"url\":\"https://www.solarcalculatoragent.com.au/guides/ev-charging-cost-per-kwh-australia\"},{\"title\":\"Cheapest Electricity Provider in WA - BLUETTI AU\",\"url\":\"https://www.bluettipower.com.au/blogs/buying-guide/cheapest-electricity-provider-in-wa\"},{\"title\":\"Chargefox\",\"url\":\"https://mwm.ai/apps/chargefox-ev-charging-network/1293614477\"},{\"title\":\"Chargefox: Australia's Biggest EV Network\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/networks/chargefox/\"}]\n\nWA EV Network chargers cost **$0.35/kWh on AC and $0.60/kWh on DC**. You pay through the Chargefox app or by credit card.\n\n- **Horizon Power's 2026/27 fee table:** Here are the fees for using WA EV Network chargers. You'll be able to pay via the Chargefox app or credit card. Chargefox terms and conditions apply. 2026/27 Unchanged from last year. AC Charger · DC Charger. Electricity charge · 0.35 cents/kWh · 0.60 cents/kWh. Idle fee · Not applicable · $1 per minute* once 100% charged. The page says \"cents\", but that looks like a typo for dollars. A Synergy construction notice gives the same figures in dollars (see the Synergy point below).\n- **Idle fee details:** The idle fee only applies at DC chargers. Once your vehicle is fully charged, a 10-minute grace period will apply. If you're using the Chargefox app you'll get a notification letting you know when your grace period begins.\n- **2025/26 prices:** These were the same as 2026/27 (2025/26 Unchanged from last year), so the rates have held steady for at least two years.\n- **Synergy (SWIS) chargers:** A Synergy notice to Northam residents says for Synergy chargers, the price for the DC fast chargers will be $0.60p/Kwh and for the AC slow charger it will be $0.35p/Kwh. Please note that this is only for chargers within the Southwest Interconnected System (SWIS). That notice is about 2.5 years old.\n- **Network background:** The WA EV Network was completed in January 2025. Delivered by Synergy and Horizon Power, this $43.5 million investment created Australia's longest connected EV charging network. Spanning 7,000 kilometres with 49 locations placed approximately 200 kilometres apart\n- **Chargefox's role:** Chargefox is only the app and payment platform. Its help centre says \"pricing is not set by Chargefox\". The owner of each station sets the rate, and the app shows it before you start.\n\nNone of the results showed motoring club discounts (e.g. RAC) applying on the WA EV Network.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"ef6a1723-2e58-4d46-a8e7-244d78bafe86","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:45:35.073Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"WA EV Network Synergy Horizon Power chargers app