r dollars. A Synergy construction notice gives the same figures in dollars (see the Synergy point below).\n- **Idle fee details:** The idle fee only applies at DC chargers. Once your vehicle is fully charged, a 10-minute grace period will apply. If you're using the Chargefox app you'll get a notification letting you know when your grace period begins.\n- **2025/26 prices:** These were the same as 2026/27 (2025/26 Unchanged from last year), so the rates have held steady for at least two years.\n- **Synergy (SWIS) chargers:** A Synergy notice to Northam residents says for Synergy chargers, the price for the DC fast chargers will be $0.60p/Kwh and for the AC slow charger it will be $0.35p/Kwh. Please note that this is only for chargers within the Southwest Interconnected System (SWIS). That notice is about 2.5 years old.\n- **Network background:** The WA EV Network was completed in January 2025. Delivered by Synergy and Horizon Power, this $43.5 million investment created Australia's longest connected EV charging network. Spanning 7,000 kilometres with 49 locations placed approximately 200 kilometres apart\n- **Chargefox's role:** Chargefox is only the app and payment platform. Its help centre says \"pricing is not set by Chargefox\". The owner of each station sets the rate, and the app shows it before you start.\n\nNone of the results showed motoring club discounts (e.g. RAC) applying on the WA EV Network."],"durationSeconds":12.705657340999998,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013eJ2BUKhtgcy87h82VEgys","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RieMXSCoER2vrWSrzVeLgD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Exploren EV charging network Australia app price per kWh Engie\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV Charging Networks Australia 2026 Compared\",\"url\":\"https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-charging-networks-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Exploren EV charging prices in Australia: rates and fees\",\"url\":\"https://costtocharge.com.au/public-charging-prices/exploren/\"},{\"title\":\"Best EV Charging Networks in Australia (2025)\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/resources/what-ev-charging-providers-are-in-australia\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/03/24/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Exploren: Charging Network Guide for EV Drivers\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/networks/exploren/\"},{\"title\":\"Top 6 EV Charging Apps for Australian Drivers the 2026 Guide\",\"url\":\"https://electriccaradviceaustralia.com.au/top-6-ev-charging-apps-for-australian-drivers-2026-guide/\"},{\"title\":\"Everything You Need to Know About Australia’s Public EV Charging Networks (2024) - EV Charge Card\",\"url\":\"https://www.evchargecard.com.au/p/everything-you-need-to-know-about-australias-public-ev-charging-networks/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Exploren expands EV charging, 114 new plugs this month\",\"url\":\"https://techau.com.au/exploren-expands-ev-charging-114-new-plugs-this-month/\"}]\n\nExploren doesn't have one national price. Each charger's owner sets the rate, and sources from 2025–26 put most DC fast charging at about 35–75c/kWh. Some AC chargers are free.\n\n**How pricing works:** Exploren is both a charging network and the software platform behind chargers owned by businesses, councils and property owners, so prices are set by each site's owner and vary widely. You find chargers and pay through the free Exploren app. The app shows the price for every charger before you start a session.\n\n**Reported prices:**\n- **Range across sources:** Gridly (2026) lists Exploren at free to 55c/kWh, with no membership. Many AC locations are free (paid for by councils or shopping centres), while DC sites charge around 45c/kWh.\n- **Specific DC sites (October 2026 data):** Published standard DC prices cost $0.35 to $0.70 per kWh. Examples: Toronto NSW 35c, Ocean Grove VIC 55c, Cairns 60c, Launceston 70c.\n- **Older estimate (Zecar, 2025):** AC destination chargers generally cost $0.40 to $0.60 per kWh, while DC fast chargers range from $0.55 to $0.75 per kWh.\n- **Widest range:** one tracker (January 2026) reports Exploren DC prices from 30 to 104 c/kWh.\n- **Extra fees:** Some sites charge a small connection fee, often around A$0.40 per session. Drivers also report card holds of about $10 at some Exploren sites.\n\n**Engie acquisition:** Exploren's sister company EVSE bought ENGIE's Australian fast-charging network in 2025, adding 230+ DC ports across 80+ sites. Zecar gives a different figure: 300 fast-charging ports at busy sites such as hospitals, universities and major shopping centres, bought in April.\n\n**Network size:** More than 5,000 charge points across Australia and New Zealand, used by about 90,000 drivers a month. Most are AC destination chargers up to 22 kW, with a growing number of DC fast chargers.\n\nNone of the results gave a separate price for the former Engie sites. Prices change from site to site and over time, so the Exploren app is the best place to check the current rate.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"b0627f97-e887-423c-8836-10d01af79bc4","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:45:36.650Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Exploren EV charging network Australia app price per kWh Engie","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QE4aWMuPgZZVffYMDHFy5L","content":[{"title":"EV Charging Networks Australia 2026 Compared","url":"https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-charging-networks-australia/"},{"title":"Exploren EV charging prices in Australia: rates and fees","url":"https://costtocharge.com.au/public-charging-prices/exploren/"},{"title":"Best EV Charging Networks in Australia (2025)","url":"https://zecar.com/resources/what-ev-charging-providers-are-in-australia"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/03/24/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"Exploren: Charging Network Guide for EV Drivers","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/networks/exploren/"},{"title":"Top 6 EV Charging Apps for Australian Drivers the 2026 Guide","url":"https://electriccaradviceaustralia.com.au/top-6-ev-charging-apps-for-australian-drivers-2026-guide/"},{"title":"Everything You Need to Know About Australia’s Public EV Charging Networks (2024) - EV Charge Card","url":"https://www.evchargecard.com.au/p/everything-you-need-to-know-about-australias-public-ev-charging-networks/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"Exploren expands EV charging, 114 new plugs this month","url":"https://techau.com.au/exploren-expands-ev-charging-114-new-plugs-this-month/"}]},"Exploren doesn't have one national price. Each charger's owner sets the rate, and sources from 2025–26 put most DC fast charging at about 35–75c/kWh. Some AC chargers are free.\n\n**How pricing works:** Exploren is both a charging network and the software platform behind chargers owned by businesses, councils and property owners, so prices are set by each site's owner and vary widely. You find chargers and pay through the free Exploren app. The app shows the price for every charger before you start a session.\n\n**Reported prices:**\n- **Range across sources:** Gridly (2026) lists Exploren at free to 55c/kWh, with no membership. Many AC locations are free (paid for by councils or shopping centres), while DC sites charge around 45c/kWh.\n- **Specific DC sites (October 2026 data):** Published standard DC prices cost $0.35 to $0.70 per kWh. Examples: Toronto NSW 35c, Ocean Grove VIC 55c, Cairns 60c, Launceston 70c.\n- **Older estimate (Zecar, 2025):** AC destination chargers generally cost $0.40 to $0.60 per kWh, while DC fast chargers range from $0.55 to $0.75 per kWh.\n- **Widest range:** one tracker (January 2026) reports Exploren DC prices from 30 to 104 c/kWh.\n- **Extra fees:** Some sites charge a small connection fee, often around A$0.40 per session. Drivers also report card holds of about $10 at some Exploren sites.\n\n**Engie acquisition:** Exploren's sister company EVSE bought ENGIE's Australian fast-charging network in 2025, adding 230+ DC ports across 80+ sites. Zecar gives a different figure: 300 fast-charging ports at busy sites such as hospitals, universities and major shopping centres, bought in April.\n\n**Network size:** More than 5,000 charge points across Australia and New Zealand, used by about 90,000 drivers a month. Most are AC destination chargers up to 22 kW, with a growing number of DC fast chargers.\n\nNone of the results gave a separate price for the former Engie sites. Prices change from site to site and over time, so the Exploren app is the best place to check the current rate."],"durationSeconds":13.977436808999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RieMXSCoER2vrWSrzVeLgD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
