{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JLu1gmv7qBeyAeoJnMj2KX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WeVolt EV charging Western Australia app price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Transperth Electric Vehicle Charger Trial\",\"url\":\"https://www.mysaytransport.wa.gov.au/pta-ev-chargers\"},{\"title\":\"Charging Fees, the Service Fee and the Platform Fee (for Operators) — Wevolt Support\",\"url\":\"https://wevolt.com.au/support/kb/charging-fees-and-the-service-fee-for-operators\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Is a Home EV Charger Worth It in WA? (Cost & ROI Guide) - Electric Vehicle Charging Installations\",\"url\":\"https://evci.com.au/is-a-home-ev-charger-worth-it-in-wa/\"},{\"title\":\"For drivers — how charging works\",\"url\":\"https://wevolt.com.au/drivers\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Wevolt - App Store - Apple\",\"url\":\"https://apps.apple.com/au/app/wevolt/id6446931550\"},{\"title\":\"Market-leading software for EV charging\",\"url\":\"https://www.wevolt.com.au/home-1\"}]\n\nWevolt doesn't have one network-wide price per kWh. Each charger's owner sets its own price, so cost varies by site. The one specific WA figure I found is 43c/kWh at the Transperth chargers.\n\n- **How pricing works:** Wevolt runs the app, network and payments. The chargers themselves belong to independent operators — businesses, councils, property owners and workplaces — who list them in the app and set their own prices. Operators can charge per kWh, per minute, as a flat fee, or with a free period, plus any idle fee. On top of that, Wevolt adds its own Service Fee, which drivers pay. The help article doesn't say how much it is.\n- **New platform fee:** For sessions that start from 00:00 AWST on 13 October 2026, Wevolt keeps a Platform Fee of 4% of the charging cost. It's taken out of the operator's payout, not added to what drivers pay.\n- **Transperth trial (WA example):** Wevolt runs the Public Transport Authority's chargers, which charge at up to 7kW, taking approximately eight hours to charge a typical EV. The charging fee is a usage charge of $0.43 per kWh. That page is about 9 months old.\n- **Price ranges from MyEVJourney (Australia-wide, not just WA):** A table from January 2026 lists Wevolt DC at 35 to 73 c/kWh. A December 2025 version listed 45 to 75. A September 2025 version listed Wevolt overall at 0 to 65 c/kWh, with some free chargers.\n- **WA context:** A 2026 WA guide puts public AC chargers at roughly 10–40 cents per kWh and DC fast chargers at roughly 40–70 cents.\n- **Paying in the app:** A pre-authorisation hold is placed on your card, then you're billed for the energy used. The app shows live availability and pricing for each charger, so the app is the only place to see the current price at a specific site.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"39e76fdc-20d9-45fd-8ea5-4180706a0f31","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:46:14.730Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"WeVolt EV charging Western Australia app price per kWh","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017snhComizUwTfZiNe6XZNy","content":[{"title":"Transperth Electric Vehicle Charger Trial","url":"https://www.mysaytransport.wa.gov.au/pta-ev-chargers"},{"title":"Charging Fees, the Service Fee and the Platform Fee (for Operators) — Wevolt Support","url":"https://wevolt.com.au/support/kb/charging-fees-and-the-service-fee-for-operators"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"Is a Home EV Charger Worth It in WA? (Cost & ROI Guide) - Electric Vehicle Charging Installations","url":"https://evci.com.au/is-a-home-ev-charger-worth-it-in-wa/"},{"title":"For drivers — how charging works","url":"https://wevolt.com.au/drivers"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)","url":"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/"},{"title":"Wevolt - App Store - Apple","url":"https://apps.apple.com/au/app/wevolt/id6446931550"},{"title":"Market-leading software for EV charging","url":"https://www.wevolt.com.au/home-1"}]},"Wevolt doesn't have one network-wide price per kWh. Each charger's owner sets its own price, so cost varies by site. The one specific WA figure I found is 43c/kWh at the Transperth chargers.\n\n- **How pricing works:** Wevolt runs the app, network and payments. The chargers themselves belong to independent operators — businesses, councils, property owners and workplaces — who list them in the app and set their own prices. Operators can charge per kWh, per minute, as a flat fee, or with a free period, plus any idle fee. On top of that, Wevolt adds its own Service Fee, which drivers pay. The help article doesn't say how much it is.\n- **New platform fee:** For sessions that start from 00:00 AWST on 13 October 2026, Wevolt keeps a Platform Fee of 4% of the charging cost. It's taken out of the operator's payout, not added to what drivers pay.\n- **Transperth trial (WA example):** Wevolt runs the Public Transport Authority's chargers, which charge at up to 7kW, taking approximately eight hours to charge a typical EV. The charging fee is a usage charge of $0.43 per kWh. That page is about 9 months old.\n- **Price ranges from MyEVJourney (Australia-wide, not just WA):** A table from January 2026 lists Wevolt DC at 35 to 73 c/kWh. A December 2025 version listed 45 to 75. A September 2025 version listed Wevolt overall at 0 to 65 c/kWh, with some free chargers.\n- **WA context:** A 2026 WA guide puts public AC chargers at roughly 10–40 cents per kWh and DC fast chargers at roughly 40–70 cents.\n- **Paying in the app:** A pre-authorisation hold is placed on your card, then you're billed for the energy used. The app shows live availability and pricing for each charger, so the app is the only place to see the current price at a specific site."],"durationSeconds":10.550228245000005,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JLu1gmv7qBeyAeoJnMj2KX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WG71cMN6bQrpj8DZXqQgym","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Electrona Pty Ltd EV charging Tasmania Bicheno Coles Bay fast charger app\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"electrona.au — EV Charging Station Customer Help Site\",\"url\":\"https://electrona.au/\"},{\"title\":\"Australia’s first tap and go fast charging station up and running\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2023/04/14/australias-first-tap-and-go-fast-charging-station-up-and-running/\"},{\"title\":\"Electrona Pty Ltd — Energy projects\",\"url\":\"https://www.electrona.com.au/projects.html\"},{\"title\":\"electrona.au — BCHNO001 - Electric Vehicle Charge Station - Foster Street, Bicheno, Tasmania, Australia\",\"url\":\"https://electrona.au/evc/bchno/bchno-001.html\"},{\"title\":\"DC fast chargers in Tasmania\",\"url\":\"https://www.aeva.asn.au/tas/dc-fast-chargers\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)\",\"url\":\"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/chargers/tas/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Vehicle ChargeSmart Grants\",\"url\":\"https://recfit.tas.gov.au/grants_programs/chargesmart_grants\"},{\"title\":\"Tasmania Powers Up: 11 New Public EV Charging Stations Coming Statewide\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/reviews/tasmania-11-new-public-ev-charging-stations\"},{\"title\":\"Segment Y Automotive Intelligence: Tasmania expands EV charging network with 11 new stations statewide\",\"url\":\"https://www.segmenty.com/GenerateNewsStaticJsps/Tasmania_expands_EV_charging_network_with_11_new_stations_statewide.html\"}]\n\n**Summary of results:**\n\n**Bicheno fast charger (open):**\n- Electrona (a Hobart-based company, address 132 Augusta Road, Lenah Valley, Tasmania) opened its new 50 kW charging station in Bicheno in April 2023. Its location is Foster Street, Bicheno, Tasmania (near IGA), Station ID BCHNO001, and it is on PlugShare (location 494062). Connectors are CCS (Type 2) ×1, CHAdeMO ×1, Type 2 (Socket Only) ×1.\n- It was reported as Australia's first fast charger with tap-and-go payment. Its tap and go payment terminal takes credit cards, debit cards and NFC devices.\n- **App options:** You can start a charge with the touch screen and a credit card, no app needed. Alternatively you may use the Wevolt app (see next panel); or with and RFID card. To check whether the charger is free, use either the Wevolt app or the Charge@Large app.\n- Two parking bays are reserved for electric vehicle charging only - one for DC rapid charge and the other for AC Charge.\n- The project got a $50,000 ChargeSmart grant from the Tasmanian Government (ReCFIT).\n\n**Coles Bay (planned, not yet confirmed open):**\n- In the ChargeSmart 3 (2025) round, Electrona received $46,000 for Coles Bay. It also got grants for Port Arthur ($47,500), Bothwell ($48,500) and Orford ($45,000).\n- Electrona's projects page (dated June 2025) says it is bringing new fast chargers to Port Arthur, Bothwell, Coles Bay, and Orford. Electrona.au still lists Coles Bay and Orford under \"coming soon,\" while Bothwell and Port Arthur have their own site pages.\n- One directory lists Coles Bay with 2 listed sites, 0 fast DC, so the Electrona fast charger there may not be running yet. Separately, Driftwood Accommodation in Coles Bay got a $2,500 grant for destination (AC) charging.\n\n**Other Electrona sites:** Bothwell, Buckland, Huonville and Port Arthur are listed on electrona.au.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"0eeaed67-5753-45aa-9807-00548854af79","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:46:15.270Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Electrona Pty Ltd EV charging Tasmania Bicheno Coles Bay fast charger app","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01C93TV9WLCgzkdwfyXBaEUu","content":[{"title":"electrona.au — EV Charging Station Customer Help Site","url":"https://electrona.au/"},{"title":"Australia’s first tap and go fast charging station up and running","url":"https://thedriven.io/2023/04/14/australias-first-tap-and-go-fast-charging-station-up-and-running/"},{"title":"Electrona Pty Ltd — Energy projects","url":"https://www.electrona.com.au/projects.html"},{"title":"electrona.au — BCHNO001 - Electric Vehicle Charge Station - Foster Street, Bicheno, Tasmania, Australia","url":"https://electrona.au/evc/bchno/bchno-001.html"},{"title":"DC fast chargers in Tasmania","url":"https://www.aeva.asn.au/tas/dc-fast-chargers"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)","url":"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/chargers/tas/"},{"title":"Electric Vehicle ChargeSmart Grants","url":"https://recfit.tas.gov.au/grants_programs/chargesmart_grants"},{"title":"Tasmania Powers Up: 11 New Public EV Charging Stations Coming Statewide","url":"https://zecar.com/reviews/tasmania-11-new-public-ev-charging-stations"},{"title":"Segment Y Automotive Intelligence: Tasmania expands EV charging network with 11 new stations statewide","url":"https://www.segmenty.com/GenerateNewsStaticJsps/Tasmania_expands_EV_charging_network_with_11_new_stations_statewide.html"}]},"**Summary of results:**\n\n**Bicheno fast charger (open):**\n- Electrona (a Hobart-based company, address 132 Augusta Road, Lenah Valley, Tasmania) opened its new 50 kW charging station in Bicheno in April 2023. Its location is Foster Street, Bicheno, Tasmania (near IGA), Station ID BCHNO001, and it is on PlugShare (location 494062). Connectors are CCS (Type 2) ×1, CHAdeMO ×1, Type 2 (Socket Only) ×1.\n- It was reported as Australia's first fast charger with tap-and-go payment. Its tap and go payment terminal takes credit cards, debit cards and NFC devices.\n- **App options:** You can start a charge with the touch screen and a credit card, no app needed. Alternatively you may use the Wevolt app (see next panel); or with and RFID card. To check whether the charger is free, use either the Wevolt app or the Charge@Large app.\n- Two parking bays are reserved for electric vehicle charging only - one for DC rapid charge and the other for AC Charge.\n- The project got a $50,000 ChargeSmart grant from the Tasmanian Government (ReCFIT).\n\n**Coles Bay (planned, not yet confirmed open):**\n- In the ChargeSmart 3 (2025) round, Electrona received $46,000 for Coles Bay. It also got grants for Port Arthur ($47,500), Bothwell ($48,500) and Orford ($45,000).\n- Electrona's projects page (dated June 2025) says it is bringing new fast chargers to Port Arthur, Bothwell, Coles Bay, and Orford. Electrona.au still lists Coles Bay and Orford under \"coming soon,\" while Bothwell and Port Arthur have their own site pages.\n- One directory lists Coles Bay with 2 listed sites, 0 fast DC, so the Electrona fast charger there may not be running yet. Separately, Driftwood Accommodation in Coles Bay got a $2,500 grant for destination (AC) charging.\n\n**Other Electrona sites:** Bothwell, Buckland, Huonville and Port Arthur are listed on electrona.au."],"durationSeconds":10.488689407999992,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WG71cMN6bQrpj8DZXqQgym","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QW3sp17CuRhD11QEqkMXED","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Woolworths EV fast chargers Dakabin Glen Huntly operator app\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"PRESS RELEASE: EV drivers can now collect Everyday Rewards points when charging at Woolworths Supermarkets.\",\"url\":\"https://getthewordout.com.au/press-release/press-release-ev-drivers-can-now-collect-everyday-rewards-points-when-charging-at-woolworths-supermarkets/\"},{\"title\":\"Autel Chargers Now at IKEA and Woolworths Sites\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/reviews/autel-expands-charger-footprint-from-homes-to-the-largest-retailers-in-anz\"},{\"title\":\"Australian EV charging platform partners with retail giant's rewards program - The Driven IO\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2025/05/14/australian-ev-charging-platform-partners-with-retail-giants-rewards-program/\"},{\"title\":\"Chargefox partners with Woolworths Everyday Rewards points\",\"url\":\"https://www.propertycenterpiece.com.au/post/chargefox-partners-with-woolworths-everyday-rewards-points\"},{\"title\":\"Woolworths offering rewards for charging your Electric Vehicle\",\"url\":\"https://techau.com.au/woolworths-offering-rewards-for-charging-your-electric-vehicle/\"},{\"title\":\"PlugShare - EV Charging Station Map - Find a place to charge your car!\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/740224\"},{\"title\":\"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/609380\"},{\"title\":\"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/245098\"},{\"title\":\"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/496968\"},{\"title\":\"Woolworths Charging including DC Fast Charging\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/woolworths-charging-including-dc-fast-charging.317693/\"}]\n\nWoolworths' own EV chargers, including the ones at Dakabin, run on the Chargefox network. You start and pay for a charge in the Chargefox app. None of the results mentioned Glen Huntly, so I couldn't confirm who operates the chargers there.\n\n- **Dakabin (QLD):** The May 2025 store list includes Dakabin, alongside Bannockburn, Bellmere, Doolandella, Gordonvale West, Logan Reserve and Redbank Plains Mountview. These chargers are all available on the Chargefox App.\n- **How you use them:** Customers pay through the Chargefox app, which is open to all EV drivers, not only Woolworths shoppers. Everyday Rewards members can link their account in the app and earn one point per dollar spent charging at participating sites. PlugShare listings say you can also use a Chargefox RFID card.\n- **Size of the network:** In May 2025, Chargefox had over 100 EV charging plugs located across 25 Woolworths stores around Australia, with more planned.\n- **Hardware and speeds:** Autel supplies chargers at some sites. Woolworths stores offer a mix of AC and DC charging options from as slow as 7kW AC to 200 kW DC. That source is from November 2026.\n- **Pricing:** An older forum post (about 2023) quoted Chargefox prices of DC (up to 200kW) = 55c/kWh AC (7kW) = 25c/kWh. These are likely out of date.\n- **Not every charger at a Woolworths belongs to Woolworths:** Some shopping centres with a Woolworths have chargers from other networks. For example, one PlugShare listing shows Evie 50kW DC chargers near a Woolworths pick-up entrance.\n\nGlen Huntly is in Victoria, and none of these sources include a Victorian store list. If you need that site specifically, a search like \"Woolworths Glen Huntly EV charger\" or \"Glen Huntly PlugShare\" should show whether it's Chargefox or another network such as Evie, Jolt or bp pulse.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"bf16e3be-6181-4d51-b52e-2553789923c4","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:46:17.295Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Woolworths EV fast chargers Dakabin Glen Huntly operator app","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DybR6a4tgsaE8HK2T5wcmb","content":[{"title":"PRESS RELEASE: EV drivers can now collect Everyday Rewards points when charging at Woolworths Supermarkets.","url":"https://getthewordout.com.au/press-release/press-release-ev-drivers-can-now-collect-everyday-rewards-points-when-charging-at-woolworths-supermarkets/"},{"title":"Autel Chargers Now at IKEA and Woolworths Sites","url":"https://zecar.com/reviews/autel-expands-charger-footprint-from-homes-to-the-largest-retailers-in-anz"},{"title":"Australian EV charging platform partners with retail giant's rewards program - The Driven IO","url":"https://thedriven.io/2025/05/14/australian-ev-charging-platform-partners-with-retail-giants-rewards-program/"},{"title":"Chargefox partners with Woolworths Everyday Rewards points","url":"https://www.propertycenterpiece.com.au/post/chargefox-partners-with-woolworths-everyday-rewards-points"},{"title":"Woolworths offering rewards for charging your Electric Vehicle","url":"https://techau.com.au/woolworths-offering-rewards-for-charging-your-electric-vehicle/"},{"title":"PlugShare - EV Charging Station Map - Find a place to charge your car!","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/740224"},{"title":"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/609380"},{"title":"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/245098"},{"title":"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/496968"},{"title":"Woolworths Charging including DC Fast Charging","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/woolworths-charging-including-dc-fast-charging.317693/"}]},"Woolworths' own EV chargers, including the ones at Dakabin, run on the Chargefox network. You start and pay for a charge in the Chargefox app. None of the results mentioned Glen Huntly, so I couldn't confirm who operates the chargers there.\n\n- **Dakabin (QLD):** The May 2025 store list includes Dakabin, alongside Bannockburn, Bellmere, Doolandella, Gordonvale West, Logan Reserve and Redbank Plains Mountview. These chargers are all available on the Chargefox App.\n- **How you use them:** Customers pay through the Chargefox app, which is open to all EV drivers, not only Woolworths shoppers. Everyday Rewards members can link their account in the app and earn one point per dollar spent charging at participating sites. PlugShare listings say you can also use a Chargefox RFID card.\n- **Size of the network:** In May 2025, Chargefox had over 100 EV charging plugs located across 25 Woolworths stores around Australia, with more planned.\n- **Hardware and speeds:** Autel supplies chargers at some sites. Woolworths stores offer a mix of AC and DC charging options from as slow as 7kW AC to 200 kW DC. That source is from November 2026.\n- **Pricing:** An older forum post (about 2023) quoted Chargefox prices of DC (up to 200kW) = 55c/kWh AC (7kW) = 25c/kWh. These are likely out of date.\n- **Not every charger at a Woolworths belongs to Woolworths:** Some shopping centres with a Woolworths have chargers from other networks. For example, one PlugShare listing shows Evie 50kW DC chargers near a Woolworths pick-up entrance.\n\nGlen Huntly is in Victoria, and none of these sources include a Victorian store list. If you need that site specifically, a search like \"Woolworths Glen Huntly EV charger\" or \"Glen Huntly PlugShare\" should show whether it's Chargefox or another network such as Evie, Jolt or bp pulse."],"durationSeconds":12.062322360999998,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QW3sp17CuRhD11QEqkMXED","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
