{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DqUp4BJd1UnPwvJVuS3j7K","type":"tool_result","content":"**How drivers pay**\n- Payment runs through the Wevolt app. You tap to start in the app, and an RFID card is optional.\n- The app places \"a temporary pre-authorisation hold\" on your card to verify it, and then you're charged only for the energy you actually use.\n- The FAQ says this hold is $25 and is \"released after your session.\"\n- If a session was billed wrongly, you can contact Wevolt for a review and a possible refund.\n\n**Pricing**\n- The page gives no per-kWh rate and no service fee amount.\n- Independent operators \"set their own prices,\" so the cost depends on the site.\n- An app screenshot shows a sample session of 30 kWh costing $8.55. That's an illustration, not a published rate.\n- Some sites charge idle fees if you stay plugged in after charging finishes, but no amounts are given.\n\n**Terms of use**\n- The footer links to the terms at /terms, with Privacy and Legal pages beside it.\n- The terms text isn't on this page, so I can't quote any clause about scraping or automated access. You'd need to open the /terms page for that."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"88406749-0dd8-44a4-ad72-bc263549856d","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:46:29.608Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":33148,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**How drivers pay**\n- Payment runs through the Wevolt app. You tap to start in the app, and an RFID card is optional.\n- The app places \"a temporary pre-authorisation hold\" on your card to verify it, and then you're charged only for the energy you actually use.\n- The FAQ says this hold is $25 and is \"released after your session.\"\n- If a session was billed wrongly, you can contact Wevolt for a review and a possible refund.\n\n**Pricing**\n- The page gives no per-kWh rate and no service fee amount.\n- Independent operators \"set their own prices,\" so the cost depends on the site.\n- An app screenshot shows a sample session of 30 kWh costing $8.55. That's an illustration, not a published rate.\n- Some sites charge idle fees if you stay plugged in after charging finishes, but no amounts are given.\n\n**Terms of use**\n- The footer links to the terms at /terms, with Privacy and Legal pages beside it.\n- The terms text isn't on this page, so I can't quote any clause about scraping or automated access. You'd need to open the /terms page for that.","durationMs":5691,"url":"https://wevolt.com.au/drivers"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DqUp4BJd1UnPwvJVuS3j7K","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EtnQyb9vtm5S6PVsast18e","type":"tool_result","content":"I can't reproduce the full file verbatim because of the 125-character quote limit, but here is a summary of the robots.txt for wevolt.com.au.\n\n**Default rule**\n- All crawlers are permitted: \"User-agent: * / Allow: /\"\n\n**Stated policy**\n- The file states its aim: \"block AI *training* crawlers. Allow AI *answer engines*.\"\n- Training crawlers are shut out because the site gains nothing from them. Answer engines are welcome because they cite the site, which helps people find it.\n\n**Blocked (Disallow: /)**\n- **OpenAI:** GPTBot\n- **Anthropic:** ClaudeBot, Claude-Web, anthropic-ai\n- **Apple:** Applebot-Extended (training only; regular Applebot search indexing stays allowed)\n- **Meta:** Meta-ExternalAgent (both casings), Meta-ExternalFetcher, FacebookBot\n- **Others:** CCBot, Bytespider, Amazonbot, cohere-ai, cohere-training-data-crawler, AI2Bot, Ai2Bot-Dolma, Diffbot, Omgili, Omgilibot, Webzio-Extended, ImagesiftBot, img2dataset, YouBot, Timpibot, PetalBot, DataForSeoBot, Scrapy, ISSCyberRiskCrawler\n- **Kangaroo Bot:** listed under three spellings, because parsers cut the name off at the space.\n\n**Deliberately left unlisted (allowed)**\n- OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, Claude-User, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot, Perplexity-User, Google-Extended\n- Google-Extended \"was unblocked 2026-08-05\". The reason given is that it also controls Gemini grounding, which the site counts as a discovery channel.\n\n**Operational notes in the comments**\n- robots.txt is honour-system only. Reputable operators follow it, but aggressive scrapers ignore it.\n- Vercel Firewall's AI Bots ruleset in Deny mode would also block the answer engines. It should therefore stay in Log mode unless a custom bypass rule for those agents is added.\n\n**Sitemap**\n- \"Sitemap: https://wevolt.com.au/sitemap-index.xml\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id"