{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G3GEXkBnEAF2ZDQQVW7DR9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"thedriven.io EV charging price increase per kWh Evie NRMA Ampol bp pulse 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV Charging Networks Australia 2026 Compared\",\"url\":\"https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-charging-networks-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Networks Australia: Real Cost Per 100km\",\"url\":\"https://revolted.au/ev-charging-networks-australia-cost/\"},{\"title\":\"Ampol AmpCharge: Network Guide for EV Drivers\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/networks/ampol-ampcharge/\"},{\"title\":\"How to save money on EV charging (including free charging)\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/resources/how-to-save-money-on-ev-charging\"},{\"title\":\"Cheapest EV Charging Networks in Australia: How Evie Networks Ranks in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://fuelsavingtips.com.au/cheapest-ev-charging-networks-australia-evie-comparison/\"},{\"title\":\"Best EV Charging Networks in Australia (2025)\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/resources/what-ev-charging-providers-are-in-australia\"},{\"title\":\"EV charging costs increase\",\"url\":\"https://www.smarthomecharge.co.uk/latest-news/energy-crisis-is-forcing-uks-ev-charging-firms-to-increase-prices/\"},{\"title\":\"BP Pulse Price Increase - November 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.speakev.com/threads/bp-pulse-price-increase-november-2025.194122/\"},{\"title\":\"AGL EVX NRMA Chargers Roam Onto ChargeFox, Will Ampol Ampcharge & bp Pulse Join in?\",\"url\":\"https://carloop.com.au/charging/more-charging-networks-roaming-onto-chargefox-simplifies-public-ev-charging-experience/\"}]\n\nThe search didn't find a thedriven.io article about a 2026 price rise. The only Driven link is an older one: a guide cites The Driven for Ampol's February 2023 increase. Other sites give the current prices below, and they don't agree with each other.\n\n**Ampol AmpCharge**\n- One guide says the standard rate has gone up to 75 c/kWh, from 60 c/kWh in 2023 and 69 c in 2024, and that a subscription from $2.99 per month lowers the per-kWh rate.\n- Another guide, checked August 2026, disagrees. It says Ampol publishes no rate card, so prices only show per site in the Ampol app. It also says the last reported figure is 69c/kWh at many sites, from a February 2023 rise up from 60 cents that Ampol blamed on higher energy costs. Its sources are The Driven and Chasing Cars for the February 2023 price rise.\n\n**Evie Networks**\n- As of September 2026: about 58 c/kWh at 50 kW, 68 c at 150 kW and 73 c at 350 kW.\n- Evie's own FAQ lists around 40c/kWh at a highway 50kW unit, up to 64c at a city 50kW, up to 73c at 150kW and up to 75c at a 184kW ultra-fast.\n- Ampol is buying Evie. Neither company has said what will happen to branding or pricing. Integration talks won't start until the ACCC rules.\n\n**NRMA**\n- No longer free. It now uses location-based pricing of roughly 55c/kWh to 80c/kWh, and the old 10% member discount became a flat 5c/kWh saving.\n\n**bp pulse (Australia)**\n- About 55 c/kWh flat at most sites, with time-of-use pricing at some sites dropping to 50 c/kWh on nights and weekends.\n- AGL electricity customers get a 6 c/kWh discount.\n- Watch out for UK results: the BP Pulse price rises in the results are in pence, not Australian prices.\n\nTo find the actual Driven article, a narrower search could help, such as \"The Driven Ampol Evie acquisition pricing\" or \"NRMA charging price change The Driven\".\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2","uuid":"b50f8c1c-a8e3-444f-a68b-24a29e4a960e","timestamp":"2026-11-19T11:46:55.279Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"thedriven.io EV charging price increase per kWh Evie NRMA Ampol bp pulse 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013GcZfnYVdXg3ZNG1miWqZk","content":[{"title":"EV Charging N